    "body": "- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\nThank you for this plugin, `mini.files` is the most ergonomic file explorer I have used. If you are interested, I'd like to contribute this example which I use a lot. I tried to do this using `mini.pick` but couldn't find a way to set search on selected directory using `MiniPick.builtin.grep_live()`.",
    "closed_at": "2024-09-09T08:11:20Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the PR!\r\n\r\nI think this type of example config is a bit too much to be part of `:help`. Especially since it mentions something outside of 'mini.nvim' :) Maybe for a future wiki page.\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned in this form.\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\nFor reference, here is a little bit cleaner and more robust version:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal search_in_dir = function()\r\n  local fs_entry = MiniFiles.get_fs_entry()\r\n  if fs_entry.fs_type ~= 'directory' then return vim.notify('Not a directory', 'WARN') end\r\n  MiniFiles.close()\r\n  vim.schedule(function()\r\n    local command = 'Telescope live_grep search_dirs=' .. vim.fn.fnameescape(fs_entry.path)\r\n    vim.cmd(command)\r\n  end)\r\nend\r\n\r\nlocal make_buf_keymaps = function(args)\r\n  local opts = { buffer = args.data.buf_id, desc = 'Search in directory under cursor' }\r\n  vim.keymap.set('n', '<C-f>', search_in_dir, opts)\r\nend\r\n\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('User', { pattern = 'MiniFilesBufferCreate', callback = make_buf_keymaps })\r\n```\r\n\r\nNote, that creating buffer-local mappings is much better to do [inside `MiniFilesBufferCreate`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/8413efde2546be4dec9ea424bc6af346a14dffbe/doc/mini-files.txt#L336) event and not `MiniFilesWindowUpdate` (which gets triggered *way* more frequently than `MiniFilesBufferCreate`).",
